{title: 620 - On Jordan's Stormy Banks}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Gm]On Jordan’s [Bb7/F]stormy banks [Fm/C]I [Bb7]stand,
[Bb7/D]And [Eb/Bb]cast a [Cm]wishful [Fm/C]eye
[Bb7/Ab]To Canaan’s [Cm/G]fair [Eb/Bb]and [Fm/C]happy [Eb/Bb]land,
[Cm]Where my [Eb/Bb]possessions [Fm/Ab]lie.

Refrain:
[Fm/Ab]I [Cm/G]am bound for [Eb/Bb]the [Gm/D]promised [Cm]land,
[Bb]I [Fm/C]am [Ddim]bound for [Bb]the [Eb/Bb]promised [Cm]land;
[Bb]O who [Gm]will come [Cm/G]and [Eb/Bb]go [Fm/C]with [Eb/Bb]me?
[Cm]I am [Eb/Bb]bound for the [Fm/Ab]promised [Cm/G]land.

Verse 2:
[Gm]O'er all those [Bb7/F]wide extended plain
[Bb7/D]Shines [Eb/Bb]one [Cm]eternal [Fm/C]day;
[Bb7/Ab]There, Christ, [Cm/G]the Sun, [Eb/Bb]for [Fm/C]ever [Eb/Bb]reigns,
[Cm]And scatters [Eb/G]night away.

Verse 3:
[Gm]When shall I [Bb7/F]reach that happy place,
[Bb7/D]And [Eb/Bb]be forever [Fm/C]blest?
[Bb7/Ab]When shall [Cm/G]I see [Eb/Bb]my [Fm/C]Father's [Eb/Bb]face,
[Cm]And in [Eb/Bb]His kingdom [Fm/Ab]rest?

Verse 4:
[Gm]Filled with delight, [Bb7/F]my raptured soul
[Bb7/D]Would [Eb/Bb]here no [Cm]longer [Fm/C]stay;
[Bb7/Ab]Though Jordan's [Cm/G]waves [Eb/Bb]around [Bb]me [Eb/Bb]roll,
[Cm]Fearless [Eb/Bb]I'd launch away.
